  - {fileID: 1879969926}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1015302479}
  questions:
  - teachingLines:
    - "A music staff is where notes are written. \nIt has five horizontal lines and
      four spaces. \nNotes can be placed on the lines or in the spaces."
    questionText: What is a music staff used for?
    answerA: Writing notes
    answerB: Changing the volume
    answerC: Ending the song
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - Correct! A music staff is where notes are written.
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - Not quite. A music staff is where notes are written. Try again.
  - teachingLines:
    - "The treble clef is a symbol placed at the beginning of the staff. \nIt tells
      the player how to read the notes on that staff. \nGuitar music is usually written
      in treble clef."
    questionText: Where does the treble clef appear?
    answerA: At the end of the song
    answerB: Under the guitar
    answerC: At the beginning of the staff
    correctAnswerIndex: 2
    correctFeedbackLines:
    - Correct! The treble clef appears at the beginning of the staff.
    incorrectFeedbackLines:
    - Not quite. The treble clef appears at the beginning of the staff. Try again.
  typeSpeed: 0.04
